  "tagline": "Low-latency MPP SQL engine for Hadoop, Kudu and Iceberg tables, developed largely by Cloudera.",
  "description": "Apache Impala is a C++ MPP query engine that Cloudera released in 2013 to give Hadoop users interactive SQL instead of batch MapReduce. Long-running daemons on each node read Parquet, ORC, Kudu and Iceberg tables and share the Hive Metastore, so Impala and Hive or Spark see the same tables. It is still fast for BI over HDFS-era data and powers Cloudera Data Warehouse. Outside the Cloudera ecosystem, most new lakehouse projects pick Trino, Spark or a cloud warehouse instead.",
